# dynamic-ui.ine — a UI that changes state, written with ONLY the current
# dictionary vocabulary (page, header, logo, navigation, container,
# card-group, card, section, button, footer, title/text).
#
# Evidence-collection experiment (PLAN mission 75): expand/collapse
# sections, show/hide elements, conditional layout are the "state / can
# change" intent. This program shows what that intent reduces to when the
# only grouping is `group` + multiplicity and no value can change.
# Every line the vocabulary could not guide is flagged with `vocab gap:`
# and listed in .agent/NOTES.md ("## Mission 75").

make page
page title "Deploy Console"

make header
header inside page
make logo
logo text "Acme Ops"
logo inside header
make navigation
navigation inside header

# The two "views" a dynamic UI would switch between: expandable detail
# panels. Today both are just sections — nothing can show/hide them.
make summary section
summary title "Deployments (2 of 6 shown)"
summary inside page
make details section
details title "Expanded logs - hidden until you expand"
details inside page
# vocab gap: "2 of 6 shown" is static text — the notion that 4 rows are
# collapsed cannot be expressed, so the count cannot be derived. There is
# no visible/expanded state bit; `details` exists in every render with all
# its children, permanently.

# Conditional layout: a different arrangement under a condition. Today
# both containers always render.
make primary container
primary inside page
make secondary container
secondary inside page
make main-rows card-group
main-rows inside primary
make extra-rows card-group
extra-rows inside secondary
make 2 card
group shown = card-1 card-2
shown inside main-rows
card-1 title "Pods"
card-1 text "4 running"
card-2 title "Region"
card-2 text "us-east-1"
# vocab gap: `primary` and `secondary` are always rendered one after the
# other as two containers; there is no "if <condition>, show secondary /
# stack primary" expression. The Mission 59 BLOCKED narrow rule is the only
# conditional any backend could honor, and it is frozen.

# A toggle would change this button's state (enabled/disabled, pressed).
make toolbar section
toolbar title "Controls"
toolbar inside page
make expand button
expand text "Expand all"
expand inside toolbar
make pause button
pause text "Pause auto-refresh"
pause inside toolbar
# vocab gap: neither button can change — no disabled/enabled flag
# (`button.interactive` documents Ine has no booleans), no pressed state,
# no action trigger (Mission 74 finding), so "Expand all" cannot flip the
# `details` panel's visibility.

# Collapsible groups: `group` + multiplicity is compile-time static too.
make stack container
stack inside page
make layers card-group
layers inside stack
make layer-1 card
make layer-2 card
make layer-3 card
group layers_rows = layer-1 layer-2 layer-3
layers_rows inside layers
layers_rows text "collapsed"   # vocab gap: "collapsed" is display text, not state
layer-1 title "layer-a"
layer-2 title "layer-b"
layer-3 title "layer-c"
# vocab gap: the group is fixed at authoring time — `group` names a static
# set of already-made entities; it can never expand, collapse, reorder, or
# animate. There is no runtime data to bind to.

say page title
say card-1 text